        <title type="html"><![CDATA[[CSS] Docs: Clarify the dual role of the font-size property]]></title>
        <id>https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/40424</id>
        <link href="https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/40424"/>
        <updated>2025-07-18T08:42:59.000Z</updated>
        <content type="html"><![CDATA[<img src="https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/27722774?v=4" width="64" height="64" alt=""/><br/>
<h3 dir="auto">Description</h3>

<p dir="auto">This PR reframes the introduction to the font-size page to more clearly and explicitly state the two primary roles the property serves in CSS.</p>
<h3 dir="auto">Motivation</h3>

<p dir="auto">The current introduction is correct, but it presents the property's role as a reference for other units (like em) as a secondary effect. For learners, it can be clearer to understand that font-size has two equally important, distinct jobs. This change helps build a more accurate mental model from the start.</p>
<h3 dir="auto">Additional details</h3>

<h3 dir="auto">Related issues and pull requests</h3>



]]></content>
